@title Electric Reliability, Jan to Sep 2026
@subtitle Northwind Utilities report to the state regulator and the board
@author Sven Lindqvist, Reliability Engineer
@date 2026-10

# Reliability at a glance

kpi Avg outage time per customer | 99.6 min | target 105 min | good

kpi Customers served | 412,000
kpi Outage events | 177
kpi Districts above target | 3 of 5 | Hills, Plains, Coastal | bad
kpi Worst district | Hills | 176 min | bad

The system as a whole meets the regulator target of 105 minutes per customer for January to September. Three districts do not: Hills (176 min), Plains (131 min) and Coastal (112 min). Hills is the worst by a wide margin.

# By district

data districts = district,customers,events,minutes; Coastal,98000,41,112; Valley,142000,58,84; Hills,61000,37,176; Metro,87000,22,49; Plains,24000,19,131

chart hbar districts x=district y=minutes unit=min target="105 target" focus="Hills" title="Average outage minutes per customer"

table = District,Customers,Outage events,Avg minutes per customer,vs 105 target; Hills,"61,000",37,**176**,Above; Plains,"24,000",19,**131**,Above; Coastal,"98,000",41,**112**,Above; Valley,"142,000",58,84,Below; Metro,"87,000",22,49,Below; **System**,**412,000**,**177**,**99.6**,**Below**

- **Valley** is the biggest district (142,000 customers) and meets the target at 84 min.
- **Coastal** is the second-biggest district (98,000 customers) and is above target at 112 min, so it has the most customers of the three over-target districts.
- **Hills** is small (61,000 customers) but its 176 min is 71 min over target.
- **Metro**'s low figure of 49 min reflects its underground cables.

chart hbar districts x=district y=customers title="Customers by district"

# Causes

data causes = cause,share; Storms,46; Equipment failure,27; Vegetation,15; Other,12

chart hbar causes unit=% labels title="Share of outage minutes by cause"

Storms account for nearly half of outage minutes. Vegetation, at 15%, is the cause most directly addressed by the Hills program below.

# Next steps

step Start Hills tree-trimming program: 210 line miles, $1.8M budget | 2026-11-02 | Hills district

- Report the January to September results to the state regulator and the board.
- Continue to watch Plains (131 min) and Coastal (112 min), the other two districts above target.

! Metro's 49 min reflects its underground cables, so it is not a like-for-like comparison with the overhead districts.
